    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d61">

                <pb facs="0174" n="62" xml:id="pg62"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/6879: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Legation in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Peck</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-02-21T16:00:00+08:00">February 21, 1935—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 21—11:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>37. My 28, February 11, 11 a.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>I respectfully invite the Department’s attention to published accounts of
                        address delivered by the Chinese Minister for Foreign Affairs to the Central
                        Political Council on December [<hi rendition="#italic">February</hi>] 20
                        described by him as an explanation of China’s policy toward Japan. The
                        address advanced various reasons for special friendship between the two
                        countries including sentiments uttered by Sun Yat-sen in a speech delivered
                        at Kobe, 1924.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Press reports here are to the effect that Wang Chung-hui<anchor n="54"
                            xml:id="d61-f1"/> called on the Japanese Premier and Minister of War on
                        February 20th.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Report not yet confirmed has been received that the Japanese Government
                        has extended an invitation to the Chinese Government to send an economic
                        mission to Japan and that the Chinese Government will find it impossible to
                        refuse.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Peck</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d61-f1" n="54" xml:id="d61-f1-content">
                <p>Judge, Permanent Court of International Justice at The Hague.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
